Subject: [PATCH] virgl: cache combined render-target and sampler-view resources

Allow resources whose bind flags are exactly RENDER_TARGET | SAMPLER_VIEW
to use the existing DRM winsys resource cache. Xorg/glamor rendering can
otherwise repeatedly create and destroy these resources instead of reusing
compatible idle ones.

Keep the existing compatibility, busy-state and external-resource checks.
Do not enable caching for SAMPLER_VIEW alone or arbitrary flag combinations,
and do not change submission or completion tracking.

Target: Mesa 25.1.9.
Measurements and limitations: pacha_docs/mesa-virgl-resource-cache.md in
the PachaOS repository. This is a local patch, not an upstream submission.

diff --git a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@ static inline bool can_cache_resource(uint32_t bind)
           bind == VIRGL_BIND_STAGING ||
           bind == VIRGL_BIND_DEPTH_STENCIL ||
           bind == VIRGL_BIND_RENDER_TARGET ||
+          bind == (VIRGL_BIND_RENDER_TARGET | VIRGL_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW) ||
           bind == 0;
 }
 
